n.py and context-budget.py moved from non-canonical script paths into .claude/hooks/_lib/** (guards.py:34). Editing it now requires a signed sentinel, in adopters too.\n41\t   - Stale comment: _context_budget_parts/compaction.py:19-20 still says the module \"is non-canonical and lives here in scripts/\".\n42\t   - Gap: the CHANGELOG advice \"re-apply the patch to the module\" does not say that a sentinel is now required. This tightens governance (fail-closed) but is undeclared.\n43\t   - Fix: one sentence in the CHANGELOG and corrected comments.\n44\t\n45\t5. P2 — .claude/hooks/_lib/_ceo_boot_parts/__init__.py:25-26\n46\t   - Defect: running each part's source executes its module docstring, which overwrites the facade's __doc__. ceo-boot's module __doc__ becomes \"Extracted ceo-boot declarations executed by the facade.\"\n47\t   - Impact: none found; argparse uses an explicit description, and only pydoc/help() output changes.\n48\t   - Fix: save __doc__ before install and restore it after, or drop the docstrings from the parts.\n49\t\n50\t6. P2 — .claude/hooks/_lib/_context_budget_parts/inventory.py:13-14\n51\t   - Defect: CHARS_PER_TOKEN and REDACTED are copied into the part so that HONESTY_NOTES can be built when the part is imported. Both match the facade today (context-budget.py:145,189). If the facade value changes, the notes would no longer describe the estimate actually used.\n52\t   - Fix: build the notes from the facade values after install, or assert the two are equal.\n53\t\n54\tVERDICT: GO Payload 7 contradicts no declared condition and contains no P0 or P1: the moved code resolves and binds correctly in its facades, is delivered to installs, stays Python 3.9 standard-library only and fails in the declared directions, and the six items found are P2 follow-ups (doc accuracy, dead code, and a ceremony-toolkit default that fails closed and has no product caller).\n55\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3c93ec97-dbe3-4df8-8078-862e1f3fc6fa","uuid":