{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011gaAAYycjBnue2vNz8XkWw","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"Rule 2 waiver, verdict and presentation helpers.\"\"\"\n2\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n3\t\n4\tfrom .personal_path_rows import _emit_personal_path_rows, _personal_path_mask_owner\n5\t\n6\timport re\n7\tfrom typing import Dict, List, Tuple\n8\t\n9\t_PERSONAL_PATH_ROW_RE = re.compile(\n10\t    r\"^([^\\s|]+)\\s*\\|\\s*sha256:([0-9A-Fa-f]{64})\\s*\\|\\s*(\\S.*)$\")\n11\t\n12\t\n13\t#: How many ASCII letters or digits a written reason must carry, counted\n14\t#: after NFKC. Eight is a WORD, not a mark: no filler, no combining mark\n15\t#: and no invisible codepoint reaches it, whatever category a future\n16\t#: Unicode revision puts it in. MEASURED on the shipped allowlist before\n17\t#: choosing the number: the seven reasons carry 60 to 112 each.\n18\t_PERSONAL_PATH_REASON_MIN_INK = 8\n19\t\n20\t\n21\tdef _personal_path_reason_is_visible(reason: str) -> bool:\n22\t    r\"\"\"True when ``reason`` is a decision a reviewer can actually READ.\n23\t\n24\t    TWO POSITIVE conditions. Neither is a list of what is forbidden, and\n25\t    that is the whole point. The deny-list form of this predicate was\n26\t    defeated three rounds running, each time by a character one category\n27\t    further out: `Cf` zero-width and bidi (round 19), `Mn` combining\n28\t    marks (round 20), and then `Lo`/`So` fillers -- U+3164 HANGUL\n29\t    FILLER, U+115F, U+2800 BRAILLE PATTERN BLANK -- which \"carry ink\" by\n30\t    category and render as nothing (round 21). Enumerating categories\n31\t    cannot close a class whose next member has not been named yet.\n32\t    Asking what a written sentence HAS can.\n33\t\n34\t    * after NFKC, at least `_PERSONAL_PATH_REASON_MIN_INK` characters\n35\t      from `[A-Za-z0-9]`. ASCII only, and COUNTED rather than merely\n36\t      present: eight letters or digits is a word somebody typed. Every\n37\t      filler of every category contributes ZERO, so the whole family\n38\t      closes at once, including its unnamed members. NFKC runs first so\n39\t      a full-width or mathematical spelling counts as the word it is --\n40\t      the same folding the path predicate already asks for;\n41\t    * every character PRINTABLE, `str.isprintable()`. That is the\n42\t      stdlib's own answer rather than a category list of this module's:\n43\t      False for C0/C1 controls, for the format characters, for the\n44\t      separators other than a plain space, and for whatever a later\n45\t      Unicode revision adds to those. It keeps the round-19 finding\n46\t      closed -- `reviewed 2026<CR>HIDDEN` carries EIGHTEEN ASCII\n47\t      letters and digits, more than twice the threshold, and is still\n48\t      refused because it renders as a row overwritten in the terminal\n49\t      that shows it. That is the case which proves the two conditions\n50\t      are not redundant: ink alone would pass it. And it is done without\n51\t      this module owning a list of what is invisible.\n52\t\n53\t    `\\r` is excluded from the FILE-level class two hundred lines up and\n54\t    refused HERE, and that is not an inconsistency: there it is the\n55\t    terminator of a physical line the row loop counts, and here it is a\n56\t    character somebody put inside a written decision.\n57\t\n58\t    A row whose reason fails this is MALFORMED by row NUMBER, which is\n59\t    the address the operator can act on, and it waives nothing.\n60\t    \"\"\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3c93ec97-dbe3-4df8-8078-862e1f3fc6fa","uuid":"ea156e8e-b21a-48b6-9c76-bfe6f3bd2295","timestamp":"2026-11-16T18:18:45.285Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.n5R3O9/tree/.claude/hooks/_lib/_contamination/personal_path_policy.py","content":"\"\"\"Rule 2 waiver, verdict and presentation helpers.\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom .personal_path_rows import _emit_personal_path_rows, _personal_path_mask_owner\n\nimport re\nfrom typing import Dict, List, Tuple\n\n_PERSONAL_PATH_ROW_RE = re.compile(\n    r\"^([^\\s|]+)\\s*\\|\\s*sha256:([0-9A-Fa-f]{64})\\s*\\|\\s*(\\S.*)$\")\n\n\n#: How many ASCII letters or digits a written reason must carry, counted\n#: after NFKC. Eight is a WORD, not a mark: no filler, no combining mark\n#: and no invisible codepoint reaches it, whatever category a future\n#: Unicode revision puts it in. MEASURED on the shipped allowlist before\n#: choosing the number: the seven reasons carry 60 to 112 each.\n_PERSONAL_PATH_REASON_MIN_INK = 8\n\n\ndef _personal_path_reason_is_visible(reason: str) -> bool:\n    r\"\"\"True when ``reason`` is a decision a reviewer can actually READ.\n\n    TWO POSITIVE conditions. Neither is a list of what is forbidden, and\n    that is the whole point. The deny-list form of this predicate was\n    defeated three rounds running, each time by a character one category\n    further out: `Cf` zero-width and bidi (round 19), `Mn` combining\n    marks (round 20), and then `Lo`/`So` fillers -- U+3164 HANGUL\n    FILLER, U+115F, U+2800 BRAILLE PATTERN BLANK -- which \"carry ink\" by\n    category and render as nothing (round 21). Enumerating categories\n    cannot close a class whose next member has not been named yet.\n    Asking what a written sentence HAS can.\n\n    * after NFKC, at least `_PERSONAL_PATH_REASON_MIN_INK` characters\n      from `[A-Za-z0-9]`. ASCII only, and COUNTED rather than merely\n      present: eight letters or digits is a word somebody typed. Every\n      filler of every category contributes ZERO, so the whole family\n      closes at once, including its unnamed members. NFKC runs first so\n      a full-width or mathematical spelling counts as the word it is --\n      the same folding the path predicate already asks for;\n    * every character PRINTABLE, `str.isprintable()`. That is the\n      stdlib's own answer rather than a category list of this module's:\n      False for C0/C1 controls, for the format characters, for the\n      separators other than a plain space, and for whatever a later\n      Unicode revision adds to those. It keeps the round-19 finding\n      closed -- `reviewed 2026<CR>HIDDEN` carries EIGHTEEN ASCII\n      letters and digits, more than twice the threshold, and is still\n      refused because it renders as a row overwritten in the terminal\n      that shows it. That is the case which proves the two conditions\n      are not redundant: ink alone would pass it. And it is done without\n      this module owning a list of what is invisible.\n\n    `\\r` is excluded from the FILE-level class two hundred lines up and\n    refused HERE, and that is not an inconsistency: there it is the\n    terminator of a physical line the row loop counts, and here it is a\n    character somebody put inside a written decision.\n\n    A row whose reason fails this is MALFORMED by row NUMBER, which is\n    the address the operator can act on, and it waives nothing.\n    \"\"\"","numLines":60,"startLine":1,"totalLines":647}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_011gaAAYycjBnue2vNz8XkWw","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
