{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7549YLr8NnjkZSvSjWE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01C65hUXRh66ddbqFMX1KX2i","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"report":"PAYLOAD 7/34 (GA re-pass, v1.4.3-rc.1..84b83324c820)\n\nFILES COVERED\n- .claude/hooks/_lib/_ceo_boot_parts/: harness_governance.py, lessons_cli.py, liveness_schedule.py, model_persona.py, persona_confidence.py, scheduled_cache.py, state_plan_audit.py, telemetry_candidates.py\n- .claude/hooks/_lib/_ceremony_toolkit/: __init__.py, bundle_builder.py, preflight.py\n- .claude/hooks/_lib/_contamination/__init__.py\nAll are new files.\n\nHOW I CHECKED\n- I read the redacted candidate tree statically. I had only read and search tools and executed nothing.\n- I also read:\n  - the facade .claude/scripts/ceo-boot.py and the loader _ceo_boot_parts/__init__.py;\n  - the two parts outside this payload that these call (cache_recommendations.py, candidates_lessons.py);\n  - check_canonical_edit.py, _lib/canonical_edit/{guards,paths}.py and effective_config.py;\n  - validate_governance_fast.py, check_contamination.py:395-509, install.sh:1520-1556 and _framework_manifest_set.sh:95-103.\n- The base text of ceo-boot.py is not in the tree. I therefore judged the move by reading the parts and the committed rc.1 evidence, not by a diff against the base.\n- GA-only claim (code identical to rc.1): I matched three distinctive lines of this payload against .claude/plans/PLAN-198/repass-rc1/diff-rc1-06.patch:1389 and :2689 and diff-rc1-07.patch:560. All three are present.\n\nCHECKED, NO FINDING\n1. Load order and name lookup\n- install() executes the 10 parts in _PARTS order inside the facade's globals (_ceo_boot_parts/__init__.py:12-26).\n- Every name these parts use at load time is defined by then:\n  - _rp, REPO_ROOT, _PLAN_GLOB_CACHE and check_governance_validate in the facade (ceo-boot.py:55-109);\n  - _classify_pair_rail_event, _failopen_rail_window_hours and PAIR_RAIL_TERMINAL_ACTIONS in persona_confidence, before liveness_schedule;\n  - the _sched_red_* helpers before scheduled_cache;\n  - every check function before TIER_S_CHECKS and TIER_A_CHECKS;\n  - _UNSET, _validate_boot_lesson, cached_load, render_digest, _make_recommendations, _render_morning_ledger_safe and _emit_task_candidate_markers before lessons_cli.main. All found by grep.\n- `global _PLAN_GLOB_CACHE` resolves to the facade dictionary.\n2. Paths built from __file__\n- Each part runs inside the facade's globals, so __file__ is .claude/scripts/ceo-boot.py.\n- persona_demand_* and check-confidence-gate-drift.py therefore still resolve under .claude/scripts, and parents[2] is still the repo root. Same behaviour as before the split.\n3. Fail direction\n- No hook runs ceo-boot.py. Only commands/ceo-boot.md:40 does (grep of settings.json, hooks/*.py, hooks/*.sh and commands). A broken part therefore breaks /ceo-boot visibly and never blocks a session.\n- _wrap_check still turns an exception into an \"error\" row.\n- The lesson render gate still drops a lesson when its validator is missing (fail-closed).\n- scheduled_workflows_red is never green on missing data and never red on stale data.\n- The new main_checkout_state check is read-only and at most yellow, so it never flips gate_pass. CHANGELOG [1.4.4]:340-341 and :479 declare it.\n4. Writes\n- This payload adds no new write path.\n- The writes that remain were already there before the split: the task dedup state and the boot cache under runtime_state_dir(), the persona-demand audit emits, and the py_compile .pyc files.\n- The ceremony toolkit only reads. Its only subprocess is `gpg --verify`, with an explicit isolated --homedir, --no-options and --no-auto-key-retrieve. It refuses symlinks, an empty fingerprint allowlist or a missing GOODSIG/VALIDSIG.\n5. Delivery\n- install_lib_selective copies every top-level _lib entry recursively.\n- _framework_path_excluded (lines 95-103) excludes none of _ceo