onent __all__ lists are built from each module's own globals (personal_path_policy.py:640-646, personal_path_scanner.py:569), so getattr cannot miss a name.\\n8. Declared conditions\\n- Condition 7 holds for ceo-boot: the entry point keeps its path, the logic moves into _lib/_ceo_boot_parts, and a hand patch must be re-applied in the part.\\n- Condition 5: these three packages are not claimed as kernel, and no kernel code imports them.\\n- Nothing in this payload makes conditions 1-14 or the GA-only conditions false. No P0.\\n\\nDECLARED P1s, RE-CONFIRMED (already carried as the claude-p06 lane notes and open in GA by the GA-only condition; not new)\\n- P1 (declared) — .claude/hooks/_lib/_ceo_boot_parts/harness_governance.py:300-325 and :356\\n  - Still reproduces. check_canonical_edit.py no longer contains a `_PATTERNS` assignment; the tuple now lives at _lib/canonical_edit/paths.py:238.\\n  - _sentinel_patterns() therefore always returns the 4-pattern fallback. sentinels_pending_gpg misses 6 of the guard's 10 sentinel patterns, and every boot shows \\\"[padrões em FALLBACK — a autoridade não foi lida]\\\".\\n  - Fix as declared: parse paths.py first, and add a test that derived=True on the real tree.\\n- P1 (declared) — .claude/scripts/ceo-boot.py:120-178, against _ceo_boot_parts/model_persona.py:6 and the TIER_A_CHECKS row in scheduled_cache.py\\n  - Still reproduces. The facade defines check_tier_a_spec_version_drift again after install(), and the registry dispatches the copy in the part.\\n  - The two bodies are identical today, so runtime behaviour is unchanged. The risk is drift between the copy that tests and lints read and the copy that runs.\\n\\nNEW FINDINGS (annex)\\n- None at P1. I found no undeclared P1 in this payload.\\n\\nP2 FOLLOW-UPS\\n1. P2 (new) — harness_governance.py:174-244 (check_hook_live_smoke) and .claude/scripts/validate_governance_fast.py:162-172 (governance_validate)\\n   - Both compile only the hook entry files that settings.json registers. effective_config.py:848-865 (count_effective_hooks) likewise counts only entry basenames.\\n   - After PLAN-197, most hook logic lives in _lib packages (for example _bash_safety_parts and canonical_edit) that none of these compile or import. Before the split, compiling the entry file covered that logic.\\n   - Failure scenario: a partial upgrade or a corrupted part, for example a missing or broken file under _lib/_bash_safety_parts/. The hook then prints FATAL and fails open (or, for canonical_edit, fails closed). Meanwhile /ceo-boot still reports \\\"N hook(s) smoke-pass\\\", \\\"fast pass\\\", and an equal effective/registered hook count.\\n   - The hooks are not silent, since they print FATAL, so this is a detection gap only.\\n   - Minimal fix: in hook_live_smoke, also compile (in memory, with compile() rather than py_compile, which also cures follow-up 7) every .py under the _lib packages each registered entry loads, or run a subprocess import probe with a timeout. Count a missing or broken part as a failure.\\n2. P2 (carried from rc.1, still present) — _ceremony_toolkit/preflight.py:50-62\\n   - _canonical_patterns() searches the top-level AST of check_canonical_edit.py for _CANONICAL_GUARDS, which now lives in _lib/canonical_edit/guards.py:5.\\n   - The only assignment left (`_CANONICAL_GUARDS = []` at check_canonical_edit.py:124) sits inside a Try node, so the search never sees it.\\n   - Every default call (no explicit canonical_patterns) therefore returns valid=False with \\\"canonical_guard_policy_unavailable\\\". This fails closed, and no product code calls it.\\n   - Fix: parse guards.py, and add a test that omits canonical_patterns.\\n3. P2 (carried) — _ceo_boot_parts/__init__.py:23-26\\n   - Executing each part's module docstring overwrites the facade's __doc__ with \\\"Extracted ceo-boot declarations executed by the facade.\\\"\\n   - Fix: save and restore __doc__ around the loop, or drop the docstrings from the parts.\\n4. P2 (carried) — mode